Hi, thanks for the report!

>  Except that is useless in practice since omitting the "this." gives equivalent code.

`this` is actually useful to disambiguate some expressions:
```hlsl
struct S {
   int value;
   int add(int value) {
       return value + this.value;
   }
};
```

Now, concerning this feature request, I'm not sure. In C++, this would be a pointer, which in the shader-world is kinda problematic. But playing a bit with DXC, I noticed building to SPIR-V the following code actually works, and so far the short shaders actually using this feature I tried seemed to generate valid code, copying the aggregate.

So that seems to be an issue on the DXIL side.
